# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
#
# Inherits the root .clang-tidy and switches off checks that are useful for
# library code but wrong for tests. Each is disabled for a stated reason
# rather than because it was noisy.
Checks: >
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix

# - misc-const-correctness / performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization:
#   these tests exist to exercise copy, move, and assignment. `widget w2 =
#   w1;` is flagged as an avoidable copy, but the copy is the subject of the
#   test; taking a reference instead would test nothing. Likewise a const
#   subject would not compile the mutating cases.
#
# - misc-use-internal-linkage: the compile-fixture translation units define a
#   free `use()` whose only purpose is to force instantiation. Giving it
#   internal linkage is irrelevant, and these files are built as object
#   libraries that are never linked.
#
# - readability-isolate-declaration: `direct<int, ...> a(1), b(2), c(1);`
#   reads better on one line when the three are a single comparison fixture.
#
# - readability-uppercase-literal-suffix: the `u` suffixes exist to match
#   size_t in EXPECT_EQ comparisons. Their case carries no meaning.
